<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="48904" href="schedule/2015/spring/PSYC/593/48904.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120151" href="schedule/2015/spring.xml">Spring 2015</term><subject id="PSYC" href="schedule/2015/spring/PSYC.xml">Psychology</subject><course id="593" href="schedule/2015/spring/PSYC/593.xml">Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>DA </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Adv. in Self-Regulation Resrch</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This seminar will cover psychological theories of self-regulation, goals, research on self-control, and models of behavior change, tailored to the interests of the students.  We will read classic and contemporary research related to self-regulation, goal-setting, conscious and unconscious goal processes, and mechanisms of behavior change.  Students will conduct a meta-analysis or experimental research as their term project.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-01-20Z</startDate><endDate>2015-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:00 PM</start><end>03:00 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>508</roomNumber><buildingName>Psychology Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Albarracin" firstName="D">Albarracin, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>